  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\n\nGradual ridging continues over the Northern Rockies and into\nNortheast Montana, keeping conditions dry. Patchy fog over western\nNorth Dakota may sneak into some eastern zones before daytime\nheating evaporates it by noon. East winds were increasing and \nshould see that continue through the afternoon hours today. A lake\nwind advisory remains in effect for Fort Peck Lake with east \nwinds 15 to 25 mph and gusts up to 30 mph expected.\n\nA closed upper low over northern California will begin moving in\nour direction the next several days. The system moves through\nsouthern Montana and Wyoming so scattered showers and\nthunderstorms that move through should soak those areas better\nthan our CWA. But we should see our fairshare Friday night through\nSaturday.\n\nA low pressure system continues to move south into the northern\nCalifornian region and is being closed off by a gradual northern \nstream trough ejecting eastward. The disturbance will lift into\nMontana over the weekend, bringing chances of showers and \nthunderstorms through Sunday. Scattered showers will be more \nconcentrated along the MT/ND border on Friday morning, then become\nmore widespread across the region by Friday evening through the \nweekend. Patchy fog or at least low cloud ceilings may plague\nmainly eastern zones Friday morning.\n\nCurrent model guidance indicate 0.50\" to 1.00\" of\ntotal rainfall, but the latest NBM run highlights the southern\nzones to receive the most with the least amounts over the NW\nzones. Localized heavy rain will be possible in places where \nembedded thunderstorms develop. The Weather Prediction Center has \nhighlighted a marginal risk of excessive rainfall for Friday \nthrough Saturday.\n\nWeak ridging will build on the backside of the departing low on\nMonday, allowing for drying conditions and an increase in\ntemperatures going into next week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n- Mixed today's winds with NBM90, otherwise all other elements\n  were defaulted to NBM.\n\n- Confidence in rain chances this weekend are moderate and\n  increasing across the CWA, although there is less confidence in\n  northwestern zones.  \n\n- Confidence in amounts is increasing, with embedded thunderstorms\n  expected to create localized heavier rain in some areas.\n\nTFJ",
